# Aether Paradise: a floating foundation of white halls and clean glass, everything in its place and nobody to be seen.
# A vibraphone in C, its tune full of sevenths and ninths that never quite settle, a celesta turning the chord in sixteenths
# like a machine at rest, a choir and a warm pad holding it, a synth bass pulsing the root and a bell dropping a ninth on the
# third beat of every bar over a soft tick. The same by day and night, as the foundation has no sky of its own.
# Original composition for this game, in the modern sound.
title Aether Paradise
tempo 80
meter 4/4
reverb 0.34
night none
room hall 2.8

